<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 14.5 trln rbls bills June 11.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 14.5 trln rbls bills June 11.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction 9.00 trillion roubles of 105-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 21074) and 5.50 trillion roubles of 364-day bills (series 21075) on June 11, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow: </p>
<p>    Series number		   21074</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     105 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   Sep 24, 1997</p>
<p>    Series number		   21075</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    5.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   Jun 10, 1997</p>
<p>On June 11, the Finance Ministry will also repay 10.47 trillion roubles on a maturing issue of 154-day T-bills (series 22066).</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry will also pay 284.62 billion roubles in interest on the OFZ interest-bearing government bond (series 24007) maturing in March 1998.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
